            <ArticleTitle>Ruptured adrenocortical carcinoma as a cause of paediatric acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>730-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adrenocortical carcinoma (ACC) is rare in children. Its presentation is usually related to hormonal activity of the tumour. We report a case of childhood ACC that presented as an acute abdomen due to tumour rupture. This is the first reported case of a ruptured ACC as a cause of paediatric acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
